# TradingView dEMA VWAP Slope Filter

## Source
- Source: [[sources/tradingview-mechanical-strategy-scripts]]
- Page / Timestamp: TradingView script `dEMA w/ VWAP filter`, author handle `shiner_trading`, open-source strategy, published 2021-03-26, accessed 2026-05-22, https://www.tradingview.com/script/d5I7yUXY-dEMA-w-VWAP-filter/

## Mechanics

### Entry
Use M15/H1 baseline. Compute session VWAP and EMA with source length exposed for P3.

- Long setup:
  - EMA is below VWAP.
  - EMA slope turns positive versus the previous closed bar.
  - No existing position.
- Short setup:
  - EMA is above VWAP.
  - EMA slope turns negative versus the previous closed bar.
  - No existing position.

### Exit
- Exit long when EMA rises above VWAP and then turns down, or when close crosses below VWAP after entry.
- Exit short when EMA falls below VWAP and then turns up, or when close crosses above VWAP after entry.
- Reverse only after closing the active position.

### Stop Loss
Source gives signal exits but no hard stop. Add V5 emergency stop at 1.8 * ATR(14) from entry and a same-session flat for intraday builds.

### Position Sizing
V5 default: fixed-risk $1,000 for P2 baseline, one position per symbol/magic.

### Zusatzliche Filter
- Trade only when session VWAP is defined and at least 8 bars have accumulated after session open.
- Skip if spread exceeds 15% of emergency stop distance.

## Concepts (what kind of strategy is this)
- [[concepts/vwap-filter]] - VWAP defines fair-value side and suppresses same-side slope noise.
- [[concepts/ema-slope]] - EMA slope turn is the direct trigger.
- [[concepts/intraday-trend]] - best tested on liquid intraday DWX FX, gold, and index symbols.

